{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1141917-stephen-king-in-awakening","id":1141917,"title":"Stephen King in Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-19T15:18:29-07:00","id":1141917,"title":"Stephen King in Awakening","content":"I found two threads in the main Chronicles threads with some good ideas. What about using SK's lore/stories specifically with Mage. I just started reading King's works having found out they have a supernatural tie in with each other. I normally base my Mage games in the New England area so this is a no brainer. So we have stories such as IT, Storm of the Century, Salem's Lot. With only Mage core and Chronicles books how would you work some of his supernatural beasties and elements into the Mage cosmology? what would you change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:46:00-07:00","id":1141982,"title":"","content":"Buy Alan Wake on sale on Steam, play that. It's magnificent Abyssal intruder inspiration and the very first words in the game are &quot;Stephen King&quot;.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I wouldn't use anything King did. I don't personally like his stuff so much. King is really good at coming up with ideas that are either unique or uniquely executed, but that doesn't equate to being enjoyable all the time.<br /> <br /> That said, people inspired by King and his works have made amazing things, including the aforementioned Alan Wake, but also the incredible B-movie that is In the Mouth of Madness (which outright has a horror writer with the same initials as a major character).<br /> <br /> Tl;dr: Find what it is you like most about your favourite stories, what it is you like, and use that in your own way. Make your own magic, you beautiful flower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T10:04:54-07:00","id":1143500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1141917-stephen-king-in-awakening?p=1141982#post1141982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but also the incredible B-movie that is In the Mouth of Madness</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... are you sure you aren't thinking of H. P. Lovecraft instead of King? Pretty sure In the Mouth of Madness was based more on the former's work than the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T10:15:58-07:00","id":1143504,"title":"","content":"To actually answer the OP: I'll admit that I'm not terribly familiar with all of King's work (beyond getting into the Dark Tower series years ago), but from my understanding there isn't much that outright screams &quot;Mage&quot; to me. There are, however, plenty of elements tangential to MtAw's cosmology or can serve as inspiration for Mysteries! Both The Mist and the Crimson King work as Abyssal intruders, and I would argue that Randall Flagg/Walter O'Dim could be Ochema of an Aswadim, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T10:43:27-07:00","id":1143506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1141917-stephen-king-in-awakening?p=1143504#post1143504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To actually answer the OP: I'll admit that I'm not terribly familiar with all of King's work (beyond getting into the Dark Tower series years ago), but from my understanding there isn't much that outright screams &quot;Mage&quot; to me. There are, however, plenty of elements tangential to MtAw's cosmology or can serve as inspiration for Mysteries! Both The Mist and the Crimson King work as Abyssal intruders, and I would argue that Randall Flagg/Walter O'Dim could be Ochema of an Aswadim, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here I only recently started reading some of his works. And Finding out about the Crimson King and Flagg is what sparked my interest. I agree it doesn't scream Mage but I think there's some kernels there to steal....err borrow ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T22:36:02-07:00","id":1143678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1141917-stephen-king-in-awakening?p=1143500#post1143500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... are you sure you aren't thinking of H. P. Lovecraft instead of King? Pretty sure In the Mouth of Madness was based more on the former's work than the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure. While the film isn't light on the Lovecraft references either, it's also clearly an homage to King, and you can't really separate the latter from the former. IT, N., etc., are all works by King that draw on the same cosmic horror genre that Lovecraft is so iconic for.<br /> <br /> Again, the film outright has a horror writer as a major character, with the same initials, who is compared to King explicitly at the start of the film. It even sets itself in a small New England town, something else King and Lovecraft share in common.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}